# rlcalloway.msg - Ruth Calloway, League for a Pure Republic (NCR)
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

{100}{}{(A lean woman in a grey coat stands in your lobby with a stack of leaflets and doesn't pretend she's a customer.) Ruth Calloway. League for a Pure Republic. I'm not here to shout at you. I'm here so your customers see my face on their way in.}
{101}{}{[Speech] Tell me why you're doing this.}
{102}{}{(Calloway nods at you, the way you nod at a man you'll see in court.) Still here. So am I.}
{103}{}{Get out of my house.}
{104}{}{Leaflet?}
{110}{}{(She puts the leaflets down.) Ten years ago I was in the pens of the Den. I know what a house like this looks like from the inside, from the cellar. They told us it was work. They told us we could leave. The door only opened from the outside. So I don't believe in good houses. I believe in closed ones.}
{111}{}{(She hesitates.) There was a woman at the League last month. Mara. She said you got her out of a cellar in the Den when it would have been easier to sell her. She said you'd ask me this. (Calloway picks up her leaflets.) I'll take the pickets off your door. Not off the Bazaar.}
{112}{}{(She picks up her leaflets again.) Thank you for listening. It doesn't change anything.}
{113}{}{(Her face goes hard.) Mara told me about you, too. About how you "asked" her to stay. The League will be at your door every morning until there's no door.}
{120}{}{(Calloway looks tired.) The Council will vote. I'd rather win in the Council than in the street. You should want the same.}

# Look
{300}{}{A lean woman in a grey coat with a stack of leaflets.}
{301}{}{Ruth Calloway, founder of the League for a Pure Republic. She escaped the pens of the Den ten years ago. In a lot of things, she's right.}
